# GitHub MCP server (.mcp.json) needs a personal access token to authenticate.
# Generate one at https://github.com/settings/tokens (fine-grained token is fine;
# minimal scope is read access to the repo(s) you want the github MCP tools to use).
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your real token — .env is gitignored and must
# never be committed (this repo is public).
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
